# A command's page, the usage beside the line, its flags on tab, and the view.
Shot help
Alt :help :http opening the command's page in the help view: its synopsis, what it does, each operand and flag with its help, and its examples to put on the prompt
Also help-hint :http typed with a space after it, and its usage shown beside the line: the method, the url, and the flags that come after them
Also help-flags :http with a method and url typed and then a dash, the flags it takes offered beside the line
Also help-browser :help's view filtered to http, a row per command with what it takes, its flags and what it does
Caption Every command explains itself: :help for its page, its usage beside the line as you type, its flags on tab, and a browsable view of all of them.
Headline Every command explains itself
Promo 16:9
Host shop
Grid 100x26
Line :help :http
Screenshot
Esc
Wait Prompt
Ctrl l
Wait Prompt
Type ":http "
Wait Prompt
Screenshot help-hint
Type "GET http://127.0.0.1:8765/users/1 -"
Wait Prompt
Screenshot help-flags
Ctrl c
Wait Prompt
Type ":help"
Enter
Wait Prompt
Keys "/http"
Wait Prompt
